WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Very recently, Katie Davis Court was hit in the face

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.240
with a flagpole in Portland by an Antifa radical,

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.240
leaving her with a very blackened eye.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.040
So Katie, thank you very much.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.280
And I'd like to also say that I watched Nick.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.120
Where's Nick?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:17.940
Is Nick here?

00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:19.719
Nick?

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.360
Hi, Nick.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.639
That was a rough time you went through.

00:00:22.639 --> 00:00:24.240
I watched, I hope you got my little note.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.520
I wrote you a note.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.320
I really appreciated that.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.000
It helped a lot because it was a difficult situation.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.440
It was very stressful.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.919
And your note helped a lot, I truly appreciate it.

00:00:33.919 --> 00:00:35.680
I thought it was terrible, actually.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.360
I thought it was terrible.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.680
So we'll talk about it a little bit.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.320
Under the last administration,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.160
the Department of Justice targeted faithful Catholics,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.160
Christians, and patriotic parents as domestic extremists.

00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:51.840
They said, oh, they're extreme

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.080
because they believe in God.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.299
They're extreme because they go to a Catholic church

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.020
or evangelicals.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.900
Everybody was under the gun.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.020
Unless you were a really bad, sick person,

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.880
then they left you alone.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.339
Under the Trump administration,

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:07.260
we're going after Antifa criminals

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.220
and all who fund and support their campaigns

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.139
are in serious trouble.

00:01:12.139 --> 00:01:14.459
And we have a lot of records already,

00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:17.220
a lot of surprises, a lot of bad surprises.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.379
It's people that you would never thank.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.500
I want to thank Attorney General Pam Bondi,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.019
who, by the way, yesterday was incredible in Congress.

00:01:25.019 --> 00:01:28.180
It was amazing, and she just did it from the heart.

